===========================================================================================
ROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS
===========================================================================================

Incident 1

Virtual Network deployment failed because the requested address space
10.10.0.0/16 overlapped with an existing Virtual Network (HTTP 409 AddressSpaceOverlap).

Incident 2

Managed Identity creation failed because Microsoft Graph API repeatedly
returned HTTP 503 Service Unavailable, preventing Azure AD service principal creation.

Incident 3

Azure App Service deployment failed because the deployment package
did not pass validation. Required application file "web.config"
was missing, resulting in HTTP 400 PackageValidationFailed.

===========================================================================================
BUSINESS IMPACT
===========================================================================================

• Virtual Network was not provisioned.

• Network Security Group deployment cancelled.

• Managed Identity not created.

• RBAC assignment skipped.

• App Service deployment failed.

• Production application release delayed.

===========================================================================================
RECOMMENDATIONS
===========================================================================================

• Validate VNet CIDR ranges before deployment.

• Implement address space conflict detection in CI/CD.

• Retry Managed Identity creation after Azure AD service recovery.

• Monitor Microsoft Graph API health.

• Validate deployment packages before publishing.

• Add build pipeline validation for required files.

• Perform dependency validation before application deployment.

